  "verdict_reason": "The adapter direction is workable, but its read-only, environment, model-lineage, and quota guarantees need stronger boundaries and version-specific evidence.",
  "reply_markdown": "Frame this as three contracts: permitted tools, process side effects, and reproducible reviewer context. Init validates only part of them. Options missing from the brief include a staged new/resume-only MVP, an isolated profile with an OS-enforced read-only checkout, and an API/SDK reviewer supplied explicit context. Choose using the required isolation strength, managed-policy constraints, subscription versus API requirements, supported CLI versions, and the value of continuity versus independent review. Also define whether “subscription” means OAuth authentication or prohibits paid overage.\n\n1. **Q1:** The reported 52 KB observation supports stdin transport. No established 200 KB ceiling or truncation guarantee; test UTF-8 content and an unpredictable tail marker. Distinguish transport completeness from context limits.\n2. **Q2:** `dontAsk` denies calls requiring approval; permitted reads continue. Exact denial/result sequencing remains unverified. `--permission-prompts none` is reasonable explicit unattended configuration, but does not replace permission restrictions. [Permissions](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permissions)\n3. **Q3:** Haiku has no documented effort support. Accepted argv does not establish applied effort; exact wire behavior remains unverified. Restrict capability claims by model, retain `effort_confirmed: null`, and remove inherited effort overrides. [Model configuration](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/model-config)\n4. **Q4:** Default **new**. Make resume/fork explicit continuity choices; consider automatic reuse only after measuring quality and cost. Default-new must still permit internal repair/continuation.\n5. **Q5:** Fork creates a new ID; the combined `--session-id` behavior needs a version-specific test. Reapply restrictions every invocation and validate init. Accept only bridge-owned parents with compatible provenance; current CLI ID lookup crosses projects. [CLI reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference)\n6. **Q6:** Enable partial messages and measure inter-event gaps. Their documented purpose is incremental output; the observed `thinking_tokens` event establishes no heartbeat interval. Keep wall timeout authoritative. [Streaming](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/headless#stream-responses)\n7. **Q7:** SDK error subtypes include `error_during_execution`, `error_max_turns`, `error_max_budget_usd`, and `error_max_structured_output_retries`. Classify structured errors before wording; distinguish overload from exhausted quota. CLI exit mappings still need capture. [Published SDK types](https://app.unpkg.com/@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk@0.3.185/files/sdk.d.ts)\n8. **Q8:** Home/parent/memory isolation remains unproven. Add `--safe-mode` for its explicit customization suppression; managed hooks remain an exception. A missing code-word answer alone cannot prove absent context. [CLI reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference)\n9. **Q9:** Accept the reported local preflight observation. Parse valid signed-out JSON with exit 1 as `out`, and probe under the same effective environment as execution. [CLI reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference)\n10. **Q10:** Published payload uses `rate_limit_info`: `status` (`allowed`, `allowed_warning`, `rejected`), optional `resetsAt`, `rateLimitType`, utilization and overage fields. Capture actual terminal behavior; scope health by authentication and limit bucket. [SDK types](https://app.unpkg.com/@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk@0.3.185/files/sdk.d.ts)\n11. **Q11:** Unproven. An init UUID does not establish a durable resumable transcript. Continue only after confirmed tree termination, validate the resumed ID/model, and never silently create a replacement.\n12. **Q12:** Separate IDs are necessary; shared-state safety remains unproven. Test distinct concurrent sessions and serialize writers to the same session. An engine-local concurrency limit cannot serialize the independently running coordinator.\n\n## Requested checks\n\n- **RC1:** CWD disposable repository/profile; **workspace-write**; compare restricted and restricted-plus-safe-mode using home/parent/project/memory canaries and a managed-hook sentinel. Settle instruction loading and finding #1; budget 4 turns, 10 minutes.\n- **RC2:** CWD disposable repository; **workspace-write**; run a 200 KB UTF-8 stdin prompt with tail marker, an outside-directory Read, then a task requiring multiple turns with `--max-turns 1`; capture streams/exits. Settle Q1/Q2 and finding #8; budget 3 turns, 10 minutes.\n- **RC3:** CWD disposable repository; **workspace-write**; fork with/without a supplied UUID, then kill owned sessions during tool use and thinking and resume each, comparing partial-message modes. Observe IDs, durable context and event gaps; budget 20 minutes.\n- **RC4:** CWD disposable repository/profile; **workspace-write**; compare preflight and child environment under both auth modes, including signed-out state and inherited routing, persistence and effort variables. Observe identical policy and expected status; budget 10 minutes.\n- **RC5:** CWD disposable repository; **workspace-write**; run two fresh sessions beside an idle coordinator, then resume both. Observe independent transcripts, unchanged authentication and successful recovery; budget 10 minutes.",
